 "details": {
  "id": "moon-knight-2016",
  "href": "https://www.ysk-comics.com/en/comic/moon-knight-2016",
  "url": "https://www.ysk-comics.com/en/comic/moon-knight-2016",
  "title": "Moon Knight (2016)",
  "description": "Moon Knight is a comic book series published by Marvel Comics. The series begins with Moon Knight taking on a new identity as a taxi driver named Jake Lockley in order to infiltrate the criminal underworld of New York City. Throughout the series, he battles a variety of enemies, from street-level thugs to powerful supernatural beings. He also struggles with his own mental health, as his multiple personalities and traumatic past come back to haunt him. One of the most notable story arcs in the series is \"Death and Birth\", in which Moon Knight is killed and resurrected by the Egyptian god, Khonshu. This leads to a spiritual journey in which Moon Knight confronts his own mortality and the true nature of his powers. The artwork in the series is stunning, with dynamic fight scenes and unique panel layouts that capture the frenetic energy of his battles. The writing is also top-notch, with complex character development and intricate plotlines that keep readers on the edge of their seats. Another highlight of the series is the exploration of Moon Knight's relationship with his supporting cast, including his ally and love interest, Echo, and his former mentor and enemy, Bushman. These relationships add depth and complexity to the series, and give readers a glimpse into the personal struggles that he faces in his dual identities.\n\nPublisher: Marvel Comics\n\nGenres: action, Super hero, Adventure\n\nPublished: 2025-02-25",
  "image": "https://cdn.ysk-comics.com/comics/6/en/9qSaMJNQpld3ZQn4.webp",
  "authors": [
